# Normalize line endings: LF is canonical for the whole repo on every
# platform. biome (bun run fix) writes LF, and with core.autocrlf=true git
# would otherwise show hundreds of phantom "modified" files after every fix
# run on Windows (CRLF worktree vs LF index). With eol=lf, git checks out LF
# everywhere and the churn disappears.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be text-normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.appimage binary
*.dmg binary
*.exe binary
*.msi binary
*.deb binary
*.rpm binary
